  "verbalization": "Ceftriaxone is associated with Endometritis through a chain of indications that involve bacterial infections. The drug is linked to Bacterial Arthritis and Bacterial Pneumonia, both of which are indicated to Ceftazidime, which in turn is linked to Endometritis. This suggests a potential pathway where Ceftriaxone may be used in conjunction with other antibiotics, such as Ceftazidime, to treat bacterial infections that lead to Endometritis. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ceftriaxone and Endometritis through its role in treating bacterial infections, which may indirectly contribute to the development of Endometritis. The integration of these paths highlights the importance of antibiotic use in managing bacterial infections, with Ceftriaxone potentially being a relevant agent in such contexts.",
